# Pinned from the real red run of 2026-07-29 with the injection applied, on a
# host with real tmux, through the environment the `cmd` builds for itself.
#
# WHY THIS RED IS THE BEHAVIOURAL ONE AND NOT AN ARGV ASSERTION
#
# TASK-K4G1D, TASK-JGHNC and TASK-FJCE9 all had to pin their sibling defects one
# layer up, because each of those was a GREEN defect: nothing failed, a test
# just quietly ran against the wrong server. This one is not. It is a red —
# deterministic, on merged HEAD, at a named line — and it was measured as such
# by TASK-J1XCB before it was ever diagnosed. So the proof replays the failure
# itself: the manager launch the daemon cannot make, and the `run_id` the test
# then unwraps out of an error body.
#
# The line number is deliberately NOT pinned. It was 6038 when TASK-J1XCB
# measured it and 6073 after the fix's doc comment landed above it; pinning it
# would make the artifact stale on the next edit anywhere earlier in the file,
# which is a false alarm, not a false green.
#
# WHAT THE SIGNATURE HAS TO RULE OUT
#
# The whole hazard of this artifact is a red for the wrong reason: this test can
# also fail because tmux is missing, because the daemon did not boot, or because
# the harness collapsed. So the signature names the mechanism — an unpinned
# `new-session` landing on a server the process did not select — and not merely
# "the test failed".

exit: 101

# The mechanism, named exactly: no -L, so the socket came from the environment.
# This string is produced by `tmux_server_selection()` (TASK-0RCRY) and exists
# only on the unpinned path; the fixed gate cannot emit it.
contains: tmux new-session failed (exit 1) on the default shared server (no -L/-S and no TMUX_TMPDIR)

# ...and the socket it landed on was not a tmux server. Two spellings, because
# which one tmux emits depends on how long TMPDIR is on the host, and both mean
# the same thing: the `$TMUX` this run inherited names something that does not
# speak tmux's protocol — a plain file in this replay.
contains-any: Socket operation on non-socket
contains-any: File name too long

# The consequence, at the surface TASK-2GS7V names: the launch answered a body
# with no run_id and the test unwrapped it.
contains: panicked at crates/orgasmic-cli/tests/dispatch.rs
contains: app_manager_release_via_cli_orgasmic_run_id

# One test, and it is this one. A binary that collapses wholesale, or a run that
# skipped for missing tooling (which reports `ok. 1 passed`), is a different
# outcome and has not reproduced the defect this artifact claims.
contains: test result: FAILED. 0 passed; 1 failed
